# Proximal carpal relationships — draft

Four original revision-1 questions extend the existing Apply anatomy practice
and protected Review worksheet for eight named, paired ISA hand-bone selections.
The questions distinguish scaphoid, lunate, triquetrum and pisiform by reference
relationships rather than label recall alone. The existing catalogue spelling
"triquetral" and its exact anatomical IDs are unchanged; no duplicate bone is made.

The complete displayed source record is pinned, including actual side, bundle,
source-file hashes and spatial metadata. Changed records fail closed. Neither
matching an FMA/name nor mirroring the other side authorizes a teaching binding.
Only the three other authored proximal-row bones are distractors. Missing or
unloaded alternatives do not trigger a generic substitute question.

## Evidence and commercial-use boundary

Primary university teaching references checked on 23 October 2026:

- [University of Utah Digital Dissector: wrist and hand osteology](https://anatomy.med.utah.edu/diganat/anatomy_tutorials/digital_dissector/index.php?add=/wrist_hand&lab=29&menu=29+WristHand&selectsize=Large&textsize=Small): scaphoid surface description; proximal-row forms; pisiform tendon and articular association.
- [Texas Tech University Health Sciences Center El Paso: upper-limb bones](https://anatomy.ttuhscep.edu/anatomytables/bones_upperlimb.html): lunate position/capitate association and pisiform–triquetrum palmar/deep relationship.

These are reading/citation references, not imported licensed assets. The tables,
diagrams, images, wording and question banks are not bundled or reproduced. Their
copyright notices are not commercial-reuse permission. New project prose/code is
original MIT material; existing BodyParts3D attribution and asset conditions
remain unchanged. No new model, scan, dataset, texture, font, dependency, service
or mandatory fee is introduced.

## Review and non-claims

Every question is a draft requiring revision-bound radiologist review. The bone
surfaces do not validate cartilage, tendon continuity, individual joint motion,
patient-specific measurements, diagnostic criteria or CT/MRI/US visibility.
There is no new imaging case, modality mapping or spatial registration.

Existing source lessons, guided tours, camera behavior, quiz feedback/retry,
independent access, scan masks and clinical PACS remain unchanged. Saved review
decisions are not read, migrated or treated as approval of this changed teaching.
Whole-body and hand practice use the same source-bound engine; this is not an
addition to an independent specimen curriculum. The owner's preview is not
installed, restarted or refreshed by this source-authoring milestone.
